    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Change the page title to a &#8220;come back message&#8221; when change the browser tab.</p>\n<h4>Translations</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>English</li>\n<li>Portuguese (Brazil)</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly, or upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/come-back-message</code> directory.  </li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Use the Settings-&gt;Come Back Title.</li>\n<li>Active and change the message.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "<p>Use the support link plugin.</p>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>2.5.0</h4>\n<p>Security and compatibility update for WordPress 7.0<br />\nFixed: load_plugin_textdomain now hooked to init<br />\nFixed: CSS enqueued properly via wp_enqueue_style<br />\nFixed: added isset checks to prevent PHP warnings<br />\nFixed: removed redundant esc_html from wp_localize_script<br />\nAdded: direct access protection (ABSPATH check)<br />\nAdded: plugin version constant for cache busting<br />\nChnage readme</p>\n<h4>2.4.1</h4>\n<p>Change readme</p>\n<h4>2.4</h4>\n<p>Fix support url</p>\n<h4>1.2.1</h4>\n<p>Change readme</p>\n<h4>1.2</h4>\n<p>Change Verification (active)</p>\n<h4>1.1</h4>\n<p>Update readme and assets</p>\n<h4>1.0</h4>\n<p>Plugin Creation</p>\n"
    },
